# issue #15 — 3 -> 2 of 648, and the last two are NOT alignment

> **SUPERSEDED same day by `unaligned_real_identity_2026-08-14-induv.{tsv,meta}`
> (648/648).** The two survivors below were root-caused and fixed: C SKIPS
> `search_best_mds3_uv_mode` at those blocks because
> `perform_ind_uv_search_last_mds`'s `inter_vs_intra_cost_th` arm
> (product_coding_loop.c:1498-1501) fires when a winning IntraBC candidate makes
> `best_inter_cost` finite — the port had no such arm. **Read the two "remaining
> suspects" named at the bottom of this file as REFUTED**: it is neither
> `chroma_eval`'s cost/lambda nor the MDS3 survivor order, and it is not an RD
> near-tie either (the port's argmin had UV_DC beating C's pick by 35%). The
> rest of this file — the controlled `pad_yuv.py` A/B, the `crop:` breadth
> sweep, the candidate-set exoneration — stands and is what bounded the search.

